course: dictionary
lesson: 1133
title: Breathlessness in health and stories
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Breathlessness is a noun, a thing a person can have. It means being short of breath, so it is hard to breathe in and out easily. The adjective is breathless: «She was breathless after the race.»
explain: Read this: «Some people have tiredness, breathlessness or brain fog for months after COVID, called long COVID.» Tiredness and brain fog are listed next to breathlessness, so all three are things a person can feel in their body. The sentence is about a real health problem.
explain: Now read: «In asthma the airways in the lungs are extra sensitive» and «causing wheeze, cough and breathlessness.» Here breathlessness comes from the lungs and airways. In a story the same word can mean something different, so read the words around it to find out which meaning fits.
fact: «Breathlessness» means being short of breath and finding it hard to breathe.
fact: Breathlessness after running or hard PE is normal: your body needs more oxygen.
fact: Sudden breathlessness when you are resting, or breathlessness with asthma, needs help from an adult or a doctor.
fact: In stories, «breathlessness» can show excitement, fear or surprise, as if you cannot breathe for a moment.
fact: «Breathless» is the adjective: «She was breathless with excitement.»
exercise: «Some people have tiredness, breathlessness or brain fog for months after COVID.» What is breathlessness? | A kind of deep sleep | A feeling of being very cold | *Being short of breath and finding it hard to breathe
exercise: Fill the gap: After the race, Sam was ___ and had to stop. | breathing | breathlessness | breathe | *breathless
exercise: «He read the letter, and a sudden breathlessness swept over him, as if he could not breathe.» What does breathlessness show here? | Hunger | Sleepiness | *Great excitement or surprise | Coldness
test: Which health problem can cause breathlessness, according to the lesson? | Sunburn | A sore toe | A broken arm | *Asthma
test: When should a child ask an adult for help about breathlessness? | *When it starts suddenly while they are resting | After running in PE | After a long walk up a hill | When they are laughing
exam: Breathlessness is a noun; which word is the adjective? | *breathless | breathing | breathlessness | breath-taking
